    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p38-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find an explicit rule for this bijection. Hint: Consider even and odd separately.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f(n)=\\begin{cases}-\\dfrac n2,&n\\text{ even},\\\\\\dfrac{n-1}{2},&n\\text{ odd}.\\end{cases}$",
          "worked": "For even inputs, write $n=2k$, where $k\\ge1$. The images are $-1,-2,-3,\\ldots$, so $f(2k)=-k$. For odd inputs, write $n=2k+1$, where $k\\ge0$. The images are $0,1,2,\\ldots$, so $f(2k+1)=k$.\n\n$$f(n)=\\begin{cases}-\\dfrac n2,&n\\text{ even},\\\\\\dfrac{n-1}{2},&n\\text{ odd}.\\end{cases}$$\n\nThe even inputs give every negative integer exactly once; the odd inputs give every non-negative integer exactly once. Thus this rule is a bijection.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find an explicit rule for the inverse $f^{-1}:\\mathbb Z\\to\\mathbb N$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f^{-1}(n)=\\begin{cases}2n+1,&n\\ge0,\\\\-2n,&n<0.\\end{cases}$",
          "worked": "For a non-negative output $m$, its input $n$ is odd:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}m&=\\frac{n-1}{2}\\\\2m&=n-1\\\\n&=2m+1.\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor a negative output $m$, its input $n$ is even:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}m&=-\\frac n2\\\\n&=-2m.\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$f^{-1}(m)=\\begin{cases}2m+1,&m\\ge0,\\\\-2m,&m<0.\\end{cases}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
